# Feature Audit: MCP Proxy and Tool Governance

## 1. Scope

This audit covers MCP server/tool registry, MCP proxy calls, approval flow, policy bindings, rate limits, scan gating, Tool Gateway policy decisions, SDK coverage, and audit redaction. It inspects `product_platform/mcp`, `product_platform/tool_gateway`, MCP-related migrations, routes in `api/app.py`, `packages/agent-mesh/packages/mcp-proxy`, `agent-mcp-governance`, and `ophanix-python-sdk`. Relevant benchmarks are OpenAI Agents SDK MCP tools and approvals, AWS AgentCore Gateway, Google Agent Gateway, JFrog MCP Registry/Agent Guard, Arcade/Composio authorization, Galileo, and Onyx. Out of scope: plugin catalog governance, covered in PLG.

## 2. Current Implementation Summary

Product Platform has MCP registry tables in `0014_mcp_registry.up.sql`, security scans in `0016_mcp_security_scans.up.sql`, proxy traffic and approval tables in `0017_mcp_proxy_traffic.up.sql`, MCP models in `mcp/models.py`, repository logic in `mcp/repository.py`, discovery in `mcp/discovery.py`, and proxy evaluation/approval logic in `mcp/proxy.py`. API routes around `api/app.py:7186`, `api/app.py:7583`, and `api/app.py:7800` expose discovery, proxy call, and rate-limit management. A separate TypeScript proxy wraps stdio MCP `tools/call` in `packages/agent-mesh/packages/mcp-proxy/src/proxy.ts`, but it is not wired into Product Platform. Tool Gateway HTTP invocation is more complete and lives in `tool_gateway/invocation.py`, `tool_gateway/decision.py`, and related routes. The Python SDK exposes Tool Gateway calls only.

Current workflow: operators can register/discover MCP-like tools, record proxy calls, create approvals/rate-limit configs, and call governed HTTP tools through Tool Gateway. Product MCP execution itself is demo-backed and policy enforcement is not yet inline at real MCP boundaries.

