## 7. Feature-Level Target State

MCP governance should be a real data plane: approved tools are exposed through a proxy that enforces policy, scan state, lifecycle, approvals, rate/cost budgets, and audit logging before upstream execution. Data models should represent server/tool versions, scan findings, policy decision snapshots, approval payload hashes, rate-limit counters, and trace IDs. SDKs should support MCP proxy mode, approval polling, and OpenAI Agents SDK integration. Tests should prove real MCP mediation, policy denial, scan gates, approvals, rate limits, redaction, and trace-linked evidence.

